{"title":"Midnight Motorbike: A Lullaby of Wonder for the Sleepless, Inspired by the Whimsy of South India","link":"https://www.themarginalian.org/2025/11/13/midnight-motorbike/","date":1763057272000,"content":"<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img width=\"320\" height=\"427\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike_cover.jpg?fit=320%2C427&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"Midnight Motorbike: A Lullaby of Wonder for the Sleepless, Inspired by the Whimsy of South India\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike_cover.jpg?w=730&amp;ssl=1 730w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike_cover.jpg?resize=320%2C427&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike_cover.jpg?resize=600%2C800&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike_cover.jpg?resize=240%2C320&amp;ssl=1 240w\" /></a></p><p>You know that moment late into the night when the body, famished for rest, is kidnapped from the land of sleep by a mind aflame with rumination, paging through the ledger of regrets — the message you shouldn’t have sent, the hand you should have raised, the kindness you withheld — until the temperature of the self rises to an untenable degree. These are <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2020/04/23/james-baldwin-nothing-personal-4-am/\">the 4A.M. reckonings James Baldwin wrote of</a>, those plaintive inner cries for “reconciliation between oneself and all one’s pain and error.”</p>\n<p>Such fevers of selfing are only ever cooled by turning the mind outward, worldward, wonderward. But the lullaby of unselfing doesn’t come to us easily — often, we need someone wiser, someone more awake to wonder, to whisk us into a chariot of perspective and gallop us out of ourselves, toward what Willa Cather knew to be <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2015/08/26/willa-cather-my-antonia-happiness\">the secret of happiness</a> — being “dissolved into something complete and great,” which, “when it comes… comes as naturally as sleep.” </p>\n<p>In <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><em>Midnight Motorbike</em></strong></a> (<a href=\"https://search.worldcat.org/title/1435753635\" target=\"_blank\"><em>public library</em></a>), writer Maureen Shay Tajsar and artist Isihita Jain tell the story of a little girl too hot to sleep through the Indian night that “stretches its dark arms beyond the banyan tree grove and the red earth canyon, all the way to the big indigo ocean,” and her Amma, who whisks the child away on the back of her motorcycle in her shimmering sari to tour the bright variousness of the world — the snake eyes and bougainvillea flashing in the headlights, the wet kiss of the painted elephant, the dance of planets and comets across the starry sky, the enchanted loom at the silk shop, the old man braiding jasmine blossoms, the silent temples full of stone monkeys praying under golden crowns — until the tired girl is blanketed in wonder and drifts to sleep. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike3.jpg?resize=680%2C440&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"440\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike3.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike3.jpg?resize=320%2C207&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike3.jpg?resize=600%2C389&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike3.jpg?resize=240%2C155&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike3.jpg?resize=768%2C497&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike2.jpg?resize=680%2C440&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"440\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike2.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike2.jpg?resize=320%2C207&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike2.jpg?resize=600%2C388&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike2.jpg?resize=240%2C155&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike2.jpg?resize=768%2C497&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike1.jpg?resize=680%2C440&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"440\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike1.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike1.jpg?resize=320%2C207&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike1.jpg?resize=600%2C389&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike1.jpg?resize=240%2C155&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike1.jpg?resize=768%2C497&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike4.jpg?resize=680%2C440&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"440\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike4.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike4.jpg?resize=320%2C207&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike4.jpg?resize=600%2C389&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike4.jpg?resize=240%2C155&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike4.jpg?resize=768%2C497&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike5.jpg?resize=680%2C440&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"440\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike5.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike5.jpg?resize=320%2C207&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike5.jpg?resize=600%2C389&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike5.jpg?resize=240%2C155&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike5.jpg?resize=768%2C497&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Pulsating beneath the story, told in lyrical words and vibrant illustrations textured with feeling, is the universal yearning for something that holds, a cradle of time we can rest into.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike8.jpg?resize=680%2C440&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"440\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike8.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike8.jpg?resize=320%2C207&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike8.jpg?resize=600%2C389&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike8.jpg?resize=240%2C155&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike8.jpg?resize=768%2C497&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>On our motorbike tonight, feet in the wind, we reach the edge of the world. There, Amma tells me, the belly of the moon will be waiting for us, just as it has been waiting all the rainy seasons of forever.</p>\n<p>[…]</p>\n<p>“Goodbye, day,” I breathe into the dark, and the moon holds us until tomorrow.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike7.jpg?resize=680%2C441&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"441\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike7.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike7.jpg?resize=320%2C207&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike7.jpg?resize=600%2C389&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike7.jpg?resize=240%2C156&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike7.jpg?resize=768%2C498&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike6.jpg?resize=680%2C440&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"440\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike6.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike6.jpg?resize=320%2C207&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike6.jpg?resize=600%2C388&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike6.jpg?resize=240%2C155&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike6.jpg?resize=768%2C497&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>This <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2025/04/15/loneliness-forever/\">elemental dialogue between loneliness and forever</a> animated Tajsar’s own youth. She writes in the author’s note:</p>\n<blockquote><p>When I was nineteen, my mother moved to rural Tamil Nadu, South India, and I spent the next several years of summers with her, on her motorbike, zooming in and out of adventures. Every autumn when it was time to say goodbye, she wrapped me in a garland of jasmine and I started the hours-long, all-night taxi drive through banyan groves back to Chennai Airport and back to my university life in Ireland. During those melancholy rides, I was comforted by the busyness of the Tamil night that flashed by; somehow knowing that the night was full of activity and gathering made me feel less lonely. The dark swirled around me like a mother’s embrace, and I longed for the forever of it all, and was grateful for everything. And the moon was always there, hanging low over the Bay of Bengal, silently accompanying me on my journey.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike10.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike10.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike10.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike10.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike10.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/midnightmotorbike10.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Couple <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Midnight-Motorbike-Maureen-Shay-Tajsar/dp/0823456625/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><em>Midnight Motorbike</em></strong></a> with <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2011/09/20/the-night-life-of-trees-tara-books/\"><em>The Night Life of Trees</em></a> — a whimsical portal into Indian folklore illustrated by indigenous artists — then revisit <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2017/01/09/bill-hayes-sleep-demons/\">Maurice Sendak’s cure for insomnia</a>.</p>\n<hr /><h3>donating = loving</h3><p>For seventeen years, I have been spending hundreds of hours and thousands of dollars each month composing <em>The Marginalian</em> (which <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/10/22/brain-pickings-becoming-the-marginalian/\">bore the outgrown name <em>Brain Pickings</em></a> for its first fifteen years). It has remained free and ad-free and alive thanks to patronage from readers. I have no staff, no interns, no assistant — a thoroughly one-woman labor of love that is also my life and my livelihood. If this labor makes your own life more livable in any way, please consider lending a helping hand with a <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\">donation</a>. Your support makes all the difference.</p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>newsletter</h3>\n<p><em>The Marginalian</em> has a free weekly newsletter. It comes out on Sundays and offers the week’s most inspiring reading. Here’s <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/brainpickings/janna-levin-rebecca-elson-anne-lamott-james-gleick\">what to expect</a>. Like? <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/newsletter/\">Sign up.</a></p>","author":"Maria Popova","siteTitle":"The Marginalian","siteHash":"052ac1be0de11784b9ef27664fbcf33da8263d0e7cb9c6e601ccd959f2d3aa78","entryHash":"de91f3c39adc8b1f2cbfc454b6f128d181670d7125a5f518b63812efc2df88dd","category":"Sites"}